              :intent "Open error bd510b99623dbc1feab4bd1a14d2470b761da1362051955ae1262a9c8fcebb89 on default (2026-10-12T04:32:55Z, agent cost-acquire, branch :agent-95bbf985bb25, layer :seon.error/normalization, type :seon.flow/exception-error): `seon.sci.eval/install-row!` threw ExceptionInfo \"Unable to resolve symbol: profile/measure\" (`{:type :sci/error :phase \"analysis\" :sci.impl/symbol profile/measure}`) while `seon.sci.eval/reinterpret-reach!` re-interpreted a caller reached by the agent's change, from `seon.turn/resume-turn` through `seon.sci.eval/install-evaluated-rows!`. The alias `profile` is the program's `seon.profile` alias in the caller's own namespace, not in the agent's context, so the interpretation of a reached caller read its source in the wrong namespace environment (or the caller's source was the agent's, using an alias its namespace never required). Establish which with the agent's evaluations on that branch, then make the reach interpret each row in the aliases its own namespace declares (the row's `ns` form), or refuse the agent's source as the agent's own error, never as an unclassified Seon fault. Proof: the `seon.sci.eval-test` deftest `reinterpreting-a-reached-caller-resolves-its-namespace-aliases` the implementer writes first overrides a function whose caller, in another namespace, calls `profile/measure` through that namespace's own alias, and asserts `seon.sci.eval/reinterpret-reach!` answers without an error and the caller still resolves."}
  #:seon.task{:name "a-multimethod-and-its-test-in-one-request-acquire-on-a-branch"
-             :intent "On a fresh agent (r3-probe-b, branch :agent-2559040ff3c5, default 2026-10-12) ONE request `(ns r3b.probe (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]))` `(defmulti area :shape)` `(defmethod area :sq [{:keys [s]}] (* s s))` `(deftest t-multi (is (= 4 (area {:shape :sq :s 2}))))` answers every value, then the reaching step reports `t-multi` errored (`:seon.test.failure/reports` \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\") and records error 500ddeeeca094b0ccd26f74c3bd90c64c2775fa762f11344b7f8b9de5ec9aec1 (`seon.sci.eval/acquisition-refusal`, \"Program row could not be installed\"); the refusal on `(seon.sci.eval/program-context (seon.db/db))` names row `[:seon.test/sym r3b.probe/t-multi]`, cause \"Unable to resolve symbol: area\". The cause is the producer of the branch's rows, not acquisition: `seon.turn.batch/write-entity` keeps `area` private (`:not-a-function`, a `clojure.lang.MultiFn` is not `fn?`) and `seon.turn.batch/derive-form` receives no write for the `defmethod`, so the acquired program holds a test calling a name no row declares, and every later request reruns the errored test (test-step 490 ms). Fixed with `seon.sci.eval/a-defmethod-is-a-declaration-on-a-branch` (options in the evidence): the multimethod and its methods become rows, so acquisition installs both. Proof: the `seon.sci.eval-test` deftest `a-multimethod-and-its-test-in-one-request-acquire-on-a-branch` the implementer writes first submits those four forms in one request on a fresh branch and asserts the program context's acquisition has no refusal and `t-multi` passes. Read `seon.sci.eval/install-selected!` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/r3-notes.md`."}]
