+ #:seon.task{:name "a-self-require-records-its-alias"
+             :intent "In an agent's SCI context, after `(in-ns 'x)`, `(require '[x :as a])` adds no alias (run 10 F1), while `clojure.core/load-lib` aliases whatever it loaded. `seon.sci.eval/agent-require` delegates to `sci.namespaces/require`, and `sci.impl.load/handle-require-libspec` skips `sci.impl.load/handle-require-libspec-env` when the library is the current namespace (upstream SCI #887, for :require-macros self-requires). Done when the fork applies the library's `:as` on a self-require: the patch `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/sci-self-require-alias.patch` (with its SCI regression in `sci.namespaces-test/self-require-test`), committed in root's restart batch with the fork bump."}]
